Answering your specific question first, then the fuller picture for context.
Columns and logic used in KBD ref data to determine if a location has a valid LOB:
Source: aa_hsbc_helios_entity_mapper, filtered to entity_mapper_status = "Active"
Columns: location_entity_l2, location_entity_l3 (location hierarchy), business_entity_l2 (the LOB value)
Logic: take location_entity_l3, falling back to location_entity_l2 where blank, as the resolved location. Drop any row where business_entity_l2 is null. De-duplicate on (location, business_entity_l2) to get the final valid pairs.
An alert's Location is checked against this de-duplicated pair list. No active pair for that location → no valid LOB exists → no recommendation. This reflects a Helios data gap, not pipeline logic dropping anything incorrectly.
Blank/missing Location on an alert is handled differently — not excluded here; kept and scored without a location constraint.
Fuller context — all points in the pipeline where an alert can end up without a recommendation row:
1. Extraction (raw_data_extraction.py, against aa_hsbc_rapid2_hzn_alert_conformed): an alert is excluded before it even enters the pipeline if any of these fail —
batch <> excluded_batch
ingest_chanl_id IN (2, 8)
is_manual_duplicate IS NULL
batch matches a configured prefix, is purely numeric, or is in an explicit allow-list
alert_cat_cde is in the configured category list
2. Text preprocessing: an alert is discarded if its text is blank after cleaning, matches a junk-text pattern, or fails the language/length filter. These are not silently dropped — re-appended to output with LOB_Recommended = "Filtered in Text Preprocessing".